        "between": [
          "The Global Plan Towards the Elimination of New HIV",
          "Infections among Children by 2015 and Keeping their",
          "Mothers Alive initiative has had a substantial impact, leading",
          "to a 60% reduction in new pediatric HIV infections in 21",
          "high-burden countries in sub-Saharan Africa.1,2 Nevertheless,",
          "the burden of new HIV infections in children remains",
          "significant: in 2017, there were 180 000 new infections in",
          "children globally, and 70% of these children were in the",
          "same 21 priority countries. The Start Free, Stay Free, AIDS",
          "Free framework3 was developed to build on the progress of",
          "track targets towards ending the AIDS epidemic by 2030.",
          "of pregnant women on antiretroviral therapy (ART) has",
          "increased considerably across countries. This in turn has led",
          "to lower rates of vertical HIV transmission, now estimated to",
          "decrease in mother-to-child transmission (MTCT) of HIV,",
          "transmission during the postnatal period (Figure 1).3,7 Roughly",
          "breastfeeding. Although countries continue to make progress,",
          "challenges remain in retaining HIV-infected women in health-",
          "care services and on effective ART throughout pregnancy",
          "and the breastfeeding period, as well as in detecting and",
          "preventing new HIV infections in women during pregnancy",
          "the identification of HIV-exposed and HIV-infected children",
          "received an HIV test within the first 2 months of life.8",
          "Figure 1 MTCT transmission rates in the priority countries of the Start Free, Stay Free,",
